# SHA-256 of the ORIGINAL BCSIR repository files, recorded before the 3D map was added.
# Checked by: npm run verify:originals
# 2026-09-24: BuildingBoundary.geojson re-baselined after the owner changed building 207 "color" from "r" to "#FF9A87"
#             (previous sha256 588f7c66857258d518e6a8714143d27970aaf9f0c8c960072660e9cfd8acd8e9).
# 2026-09-24: duplicate data files removed. The root copies of BCSIRBoundary, BuildingBoundary, ConnectedRoad,
#             ConnectedRoadsDrawingVersion, InternalBoundary and Pathway (.geojson) duplicated public/data/; their
#             geometry and attributes are fingerprinted in original-data-fingerprints.json and checked by npm test.
#             ConnectedRoads/v0/r2.json was byte-identical to public/data/ConnectedRoads/v0/r2.json; the routing
#             network is now checked at that path (same sha256). SrcDriveQMapBCSIR.qgz re-baselined: its six GeoJSON
#             layer paths now point to ./public/data/ (previous sha256 7ccd13b97eeea5d34280aea75f4dbcb321a8c3b14393e65b5673be7620d29e4a).
#             A zip of the removed files is in backup/ (ignored by git).
# 2026-10-02: one folder per organisation. BCSIR's datasets moved from public/data/ to public/data/bcsir/ (models to
#             public/models/bcsir/, photos to public/image/bcsir/); the files themselves are unchanged, so the routing
#             network keeps its sha256 at its new path. SrcDriveQMapBCSIR.qgz re-baselined: its six GeoJSON layer paths
#             now point to ./public/data/bcsir/ (previous sha256 7a7a671350f60ca7d1204c861ceb59fee7b1818f59edf85fea6dcd950ef1a84d).
#             ReadMeColor.md (the QGIS colour list, also in src/config.js BUILDING_CATEGORIES) and main_QRCode.zip (the
#             Python QR helper of the old site) were removed at the owner's request as unused; both remain in git history.
